Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: pl330: drop only the runtime PM reference a channel holds

pl330_tasklet() dropped a runtime PM reference whenever the channel's
work list was empty, without checking that the channel still held one.
pl330_terminate_all() drops the reference too (power_down = pch->active)
and clears pch->active. If a completion had scheduled the tasklet before
a client terminated the channel, the tasklet then ran with an empty work
list and dropped the reference a second time: "Runtime PM usage count
underflow", after which the controller could autosuspend while in use.

Powkiddy A12 (RK3128, dw_mmc with external PL330 DMA, TEST_LOG tests 22
and 27): under combined SD and USB/Wi-Fi load the dw_mmc error path
terminated the channel; both pstore captures show the underflow, then
"pl330_update:1678 Unexpected!", "Failed to get external DMA channel"
and a NULL dereference in dw_mci_edmac_{start,stop}_dma. The A12 runs
the SD card in PIO since; this is a candidate fix to restore DMA.

Take power_down from pch->active, as pl330_terminate_all() does, so each
reference taken in pl330_issue_pending() is dropped exactly once.

--- a/drivers/dma/pl330.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/pl330.c
@@ -2089,7 +2089,12 @@ static void pl330_tasklet(struct tasklet_struct *t)
 		spin_lock(&pch->thread->dmac->lock);
 		_stop(pch->thread);
 		spin_unlock(&pch->thread->dmac->lock);
-		power_down = true;
+		/*
+		 * Drop the runtime PM reference only if this channel still
+		 * holds it: pl330_terminate_all() may already have dropped it
+		 * while this tasklet was scheduled.
+		 */
+		power_down = pch->active;
 		pch->active = false;
 	} else {
 		/* Make sure the PL330 Channel thread is active */
